# Build context for apps/server/Dockerfile ONLY. BuildKit prefers `<Dockerfile>.dockerignore`
# over the root `/.dockerignore`, and that root file is NOT shareable here on purpose: its
# `!packages/…` lines are pinned by a workspace test to be EXACTLY the worker's compile
# closure, so admitting `packages/services`/`packages/api` there would either break that
# guard or, worse, quietly widen the worker's boundary — the exact three-edit dissolution the
# guard exists to refuse. Two images, two closures, two allow-lists.
#
# Same discipline as the root file: DENY EVERYTHING, RE-ADMIT THE BUILD'S INPUTS. This app's
# transitive project-reference closure is core, db, db-mail (via db), services, api — the list
# this app's tsconfig references imply — plus every workspace manifest, because
# `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` validates the lockfile against ALL importers it finds.
*

!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml
!tsconfig.json
!tsconfig.base.json
!apps/*/package.json
!packages/*/package.json

!apps/server
!packages/core
!packages/db
!packages/db-mail
!packages/services
!packages/api

# …minus anything inside them that must never be copied in. `dist/` + `*.tsbuildinfo` are the
# load-bearing pair: a stale laptop dist/ plus its buildinfo makes `tsc -b` emit nothing, and
# the image must ALWAYS compile from source.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/.DS_Store
**/.claude
**/test

# Secrets never enter an image layer; every value arrives as a compose/service variable.
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.env
